# Testing & TDD Policy

TDD is the default for new behavior. Write the test first, implement the minimum to pass, refactor with tests green.

## TDD Flow

1. Write the failing test first. Confirm it fails for the intended reason.
2. Write the minimum code to pass.
3. Refactor with tests still green.
4. Wire the change end-to-end (see `no-scaffold-code.mdc`).
5. Update docs if behavior changed.

Skip TDD only for: trivial stylistic tweaks, pure docs changes, or when the user explicitly says "no TDD".

## Required Tests for New Code

- Every new pure function gets at least one happy-path + one edge-case test.
- Every new API route handler gets a request/response shape test.
- Every new component with logic gets a behavior test.
- Mock external APIs and services. Do not hit real APIs in unit tests.

## Pre-Merge Verification

Before marking work complete:

- [ ] Full test suite passes
- [ ] Type checker passes (if applicable)
- [ ] Linter clean on all changed files
- [ ] Integration traced end-to-end

## Rationalization Prevention

| Excuse | Reality |
|--------|---------|
| "It's a one-line fix" | One-line fixes regress. Add the test. |
| "The behavior is obvious" | If it is obvious, the test is easy. Write it. |
| "I'll add tests in a follow-up" | Follow-ups never come. Test now. |
| "I ran it manually" | Manual runs are not reproducible. Automate. |
